    <string name="lock_sounds_title">Lock sounds</string>
    <string name="force_play">Force-play lock sounds</string>
    <string name="force_play_desc">Sound Tweaks plays the lock, unlock and trusted-device sounds at the media volume; they are audible even when the phone is silent or vibrating.</string>
    <string name="force_play_note">When off (default) Android\'s own mechanism is used and nothing is touched. When on, a hook is added to SystemUI; the sound is played with SoundPool (the engine the stock lock sound also uses). If the “Lock screen sounds” switch is off or the media volume is 0, the stock behavior is used.</string>
    <string name="headphones">Headphones</string>
    <string name="hp_warning_off">Turn off the headphone volume warning</string>
    <string name="hp_warning_desc">The “loud volume can damage your hearing” warning shown after a reboot will not appear.</string>
    <string name="hp_warning_note">The system re-enables this warning at every boot. While this is on, the three audio properties that enable it are turned off at every boot by a tiny script in /data/adb/soundtweaks; no hook is added to the system. If you turn it off the script is deleted and the warning returns from the next boot. Listening at high volume for a long time can damage your hearing.</string>
